    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "addrman, rpc: classify linked-IPv4 addresses consistently",
    "user": {
      "login": "brunoerg",
      "id": 19480819,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDgwODE5",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19480819?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/brunoerg",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Some addresses can be an IPv6 ones with an embedded IPv4 address belongs to. `AddrMan::Size()`, and so the per-network counts in `getaddrmaninfo`, use `GetNetwork()`, which returns ipv6 for these addresses. However, the network filter in `GetAddr_()` and the network / source_network labels in `getnodeaddresses` and `getrawaddrman` use `GetNetClass()`, which returns ipv4 for them.\n\nSo on master, for example, for a node whose addrman holds a 6to4 or Teredo address:\n  - getaddrmaninfo counts it under ipv6.\n  - getnodeaddresses 0 \"ipv6\" doesn't return it.\n  - getnodeaddresses 0 \"ipv4\" does return it, labelled ipv4.\n\nThis PR changes all of this places to use `GetNetwork()`. This way the filter, labels and the counts agree. We should leave `GetNetClass()` usage for netgroup and bucketing decisions, where treating linked-IPv4 addresses as IPv4 is intended. If you pick the change in the fuzz target and run it without the other changes, it's expected to crash to reproduce the issue.\n",
