      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "On master, I reproduced that `getaddrmaninfo` counts a 6to4 address as ipv6, while `getnodeaddresses` treats it as ipv4. On b7eeb2d, I confirmed that both now report it as ipv6.\r\n\r\nI checked the callers of `GetAddressesUnsafe`. `getaddr` passes `nullopt`, so it is unaffected, and since `ASMapHealthCheck()` combines the IPv4 and IPv6 results, my reading is that its totals should not change.\r\n\r\nAccording to the code and the release note, linked-IPv4 addresses are still shown as ipv4 in `getpeerinfo` after this PR. Since the RPCs that deal with addrman are now consistent with each other, I think this difference is acceptable.\r\n\r\nI have not run the fuzz tests, and I have not checked `getpeerinfo` with real connections or tested with NAT64 / RFC6145 addresses.",
